{"type":"message","id":"fe04d723","parentId":"42899338","timestamp":"2026-04-15T10:44:41.677Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_81ehnd55snku_1","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"clawhub.ai price scraper skill\",\n  \"provider\": \"miaoda\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"price-monitor for Openclaw\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.toolify.ai/openclaw-skills/price-monitor-19693\",\n      \"description\": \"It eliminates the need for manual site checks by providing a programmable framework to watch for specific triggers, such as price drops or restock events, ensuring you never miss...\\nMonitoring product price drops on major e-commerce platforms like Amazon or Best Buy.\\nReceiving instant notifications when high-demand, out-of-stock items become available.\\nBuilding a comprehensive historical price database for market analysis and trend forecasting.\\nTracking competitor website changes, promotional updates, or new product launches automatically.\\nHow price-monitor Works\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Price Tracker\",\n      \"url\": \"https://clawhub.ai/Michael-laffin/price-tracker\",\n      \"description\": \"Example Request: \\\"Find Nintendo Switch bundles where eBay price is 20%+ higher than Amazon, accounting for all fees...\\nExport historical data for analysis\\nExample Request: \\\"Show me the price history for AirPods Pro 2 over the last 60 days. Identify the best buying window.\\\"\\n4. Automated Alerts\\nAlert Configuration:\\nPrice drop alerts (below threshold)\\nArbitrage opportunity alerts (margin threshold)\\nCompetitor price alerts (when competitor lowers price)\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Web Scraper Skill (Apify + Firecrawl) for Openclaw\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.toolify.ai/openclaw-skills/web-scraper-skill-21870\",\n      \"description\": \"By integrating Firecrawl and Apify, Openclaw Skills users can convert any website into structured JSON or clean markdown. Firecrawl is optimized for crawling and providing LLM-friendly content, while Apify offers specialized Actors for complex targets like social media, Google Maps, and e-commerce platforms. This ensures your agent has access to real-time web data for research, analysis, or content generation pipelines.\\nWeb Scraper Skill (Apify + Firecrawl) Use Cases\\nSc...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"ClawHub\",\n      \"url\": \"https://openclaw-ai.com/en/docs/tools/clawhub\",\n      \"description\": \"Update skills later with...\\n<beginning of the code>clawhub install my-skill-pack<end of the code>\\nUpdate installed skills\\n<beginning of the code>clawhub update --all<end of the code>\\nBack up your skills (publish or sync)\\nFor a single skill folder:\\n<beginning of the code>clawhub publish ./my-skill --slug my-skill --name \\\"My Skill\\\" --version 1.0.\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"OpenClaw爬虫实战:3 分钟搞定价格数据采集_如何让openclaw抓取携程房价-CSDN博客\",\n      \"url\": \"https://blog.csdn.net/globaldiamond/article/details/159803079\",\n      \"description\": \"而 OpenClaw 的出现，让这些重复动作变成一句话命令就能完成的自动化流程。\\n更重要的是，新手无需懂代码，也可以像“开灯”一样轻松让它工作。\\n它就能自动安装技能 → 自动完成任务 → 自动生成结果 → 自动推送到你的微信...\\n• curl-http：适合简单网页、请求速度快\\n• playwright-scraper-skill：支持 JS 渲染，适合动态页面、电商类网站\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"OpenClaw Skills for Marketing: 15 Must-Have Tools for 2026\",\n      \"url\": \"https://clawoneclick.com/en/blog/openclaw-skills-marketing-guide\",\n      \"description\": \"With 3,286 skills available on ClawHub after the February 2026 security cleanup, marketers can automate keyword research, content creation, rank tracking, and campaign management without switching between expensive tools.\\nTop 15 OpenClaw Skills for Marketing\\nThese skills are sourced from ClawHub rankings, the awesome-openclaw-skills curated list, and community recommendations. Each skill is verified as safe and actively maintained. For a broader look at trending skills across all...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"claw0x\",\n      \"url\": \"https://rankinpublic.xyz/products/claw0x.com\",\n      \"description\": \"Not another SaaS dashboard. A pay-per-call skills layer built for autonomous software.\\nAtomic Billing\\nAgents pay $0.001 per successful call, not $500/mo. Zero waste, zero idle fees.\\nOne Unified Gateway\\nOne key connects your OpenClaw or LangChain agent to thousands of skills. No multiple vendor setups.\\nAuto Quality Control\\n✓ Skill downloaded to ./skills/twitter_scraper/\\n✓ claw0x...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Claude MCP Skill\",\n      \"url\": \"https://docs.scraperapi.com/integrations/llm-integrations/claude-mcp-skill\",\n      \"description\": \"Without it, you can still call the MCP tools by using the <beginning of the code>scrape<end of the code> keyword and specifying parameters like url, country_code, render, etc.\\nThe skill helps your agent choose between the various ScraperAPI tools (scrape, google_search, amazon_search, etc.) based on the task. For example, it suggests using <beginning of the code>google_search<end of the code> for research or...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"ClawHub.aiの解説：22万スターOpenClawの公式スキルストア、3000以上のスキルでAIエージェントを拡張する方法\",\n      \"url\": \"https://help.apiyi.com/ja/clawhub-ai-openclaw-skills-registry-guide-ja.html\",\n      \"description\": \"ClawHub（clawhub.ai）は、OpenClaw チームによって構築・維持されている公式のスキルレジストリ です。ClawHub は OpenClaw の公式スキルストア ：3,286 以上の Skills、セマンティック検索、CLI ツールに...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"10 Best OpenClaw Skills for Founders and Entrepreneurs in 2026\",\n      \"url\": \"https://superframeworks.com/articles/best-openclaw-skills-founders\",\n      \"description\": \"OpenClaw itself is free and open source. The main cost is the LLM API usage — founders report spending $400–$500/month for heavy daily use with Claude. Most skills are free, though some premium ones on ClawHub cost $10–$200. You’ll also need API keys for services like Firecrawl, HubSpot, and Google Cloud, which have their own pricing. For a solo founder using it moderately, expect $...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"query":"clawhub.ai price scraper skill","provider":"miaoda","count":10,"results":[{"title":"price-monitor for Openclaw","url":"https://www.toolify.ai/openclaw-skills/price-monitor-19693","description":"It eliminates the need for manual site checks by providing a programmable framework to watch for specific triggers, such as price drops or restock events, ensuring you never miss...\nMonitoring product price drops on major e-commerce platforms like Amazon or Best Buy.\nReceiving instant notifications when high-demand, out-of-stock items become available.\nBuilding a comprehensive historical price database for market analysis and trend forecasting.\nTracking competitor website changes, promotional updates, or new product launches automatically.\nHow price-monitor Works\n","siteName":""},{"title":"Price Tracker","url":"https://clawhub.ai/Michael-laffin/price-tracker","description":"Example Request: \"Find Nintendo Switch bundles where eBay price is 20%+ higher than Amazon, accounting for all fees...\nExport historical data for analysis\nExample Request: \"Show me the price history for AirPods Pro 2 over the last 60 days. Identify the best buying window.\"\n4. Automated Alerts\nAlert Configuration:\nPrice drop alerts (below threshold)\nArbitrage opportunity alerts (margin threshold)\nCompetitor price alerts (when competitor lowers price)\n","siteName":""},{"title":"Web Scraper Skill (Apify + Firecrawl) for Openclaw","url":"https://www.toolify.ai/openclaw-skills/web-scraper-skill-21870","description":"By integrating Firecrawl and Apify, Openclaw Skills users can convert any website into structured JSON or clean markdown. Firecrawl is optimized for crawling and providing LLM-friendly content, while Apify offers specialized Actors for complex targets like social media, Google Maps, and e-commerce platforms. This ensures your agent has access to real-time web data for research, analysis, or content generation pipelines.\nWeb Scraper Skill (Apify + Firecrawl) Use Cases\nSc...\n","siteName":""},{"title":"ClawHub","url":"https://openclaw-ai.com/en/docs/tools/clawhub","description":"Update skills later with...\n<beginning of the code>clawhub install my-skill-pack<end of the code>\nUpdate installed skills\n<beginning of the code>clawhub update --all<end of the code>\nBack up your skills (publish or sync)\nFor a single skill folder:\n<beginning of the code>clawhub publish ./my-skill --slug my-skill --name \"My Skill\" --version 1.0.","siteName":""},{"title":"OpenClaw爬虫实战:3 分钟搞定价格数据采集_如何让openclaw抓取携程房价-CSDN博客","url":"https://blog.csdn.net/globaldiamond/article/details/159803079","description":"而 OpenClaw 的出现，让这些重复动作变成一句话命令就能完成的自动化流程。\n更重要的是，新手无需懂代码，也可以像“开灯”一样轻松让它工作。\n它就能自动安装技能 → 自动完成任务 → 自动生成结果 → 自动推送到你的微信...\n• curl-http：适合简单网页、请求速度快\n• playwright-scraper-skill：支持 JS 渲染，适合动态页面、电商类网站\n","siteName":""},{"title":"OpenClaw Skills for Marketing: 15 Must-Have Tools for 2026","url":"https://clawoneclick.com/en/blog/openclaw-skills-marketing-guide","description":"With 3,286 skills available on ClawHub after the February 2026 security cleanup, marketers can automate keyword research, content creation, rank tracking, and campaign management without switching between expensive tools.\nTop 15 OpenClaw Skills for Marketing\nThese skills are sourced from ClawHub rankings, the awesome-openclaw-skills curated list, and community recommendations. Each skill is verified as safe and actively maintained. For a broader look at trending skills across all...\n","siteName":""},{"title":"claw0x","url":"https://rankinpublic.xyz/products/claw0x.com","description":"Not another SaaS dashboard. A pay-per-call skills layer built for autonomous software.\nAtomic Billing\nAgents pay $0.001 per successful call, not $500/mo. Zero waste, zero idle fees.\nOne Unified Gateway\nOne key connects your OpenClaw or LangChain agent to thousands of skills. No multiple vendor setups.\nAuto Quality Control\n✓ Skill downloaded to ./skills/twitter_scraper/\n✓ claw0x...\n","siteName":""},{"title":"Claude MCP Skill","url":"https://docs.scraperapi.com/integrations/llm-integrations/claude-mcp-skill","description":"Without it, you can still call the MCP tools by using the <beginning of the code>scrape<end of the code> keyword and specifying parameters like url, country_code, render, etc.\nThe skill helps your agent choose between the various ScraperAPI tools (scrape, google_search, amazon_search, etc.) based on the task. For example, it suggests using <beginning of the code>google_search<end of the code> for research or...\n","siteName":""},{"title":"ClawHub.aiの解説：22万スターOpenClawの公式スキルストア、3000以上のスキルでAIエージェントを拡張する方法","url":"https://help.apiyi.com/ja/clawhub-ai-openclaw-skills-registry-guide-ja.html","description":"ClawHub（clawhub.ai）は、OpenClaw チームによって構築・維持されている公式のスキルレジストリ です。ClawHub は OpenClaw の公式スキルストア ：3,286 以上の Skills、セマンティック検索、CLI ツールに...\n","siteName":""},{"title":"10 Best OpenClaw Skills for Founders and Entrepreneurs in 2026","url":"https://superframeworks.com/articles/best-openclaw-skills-founders","description":"OpenClaw itself is free and open source. The main cost is the LLM API usage — founders report spending $400–$500/month for heavy daily use with Claude. Most skills are free, though some premium ones on ClawHub cost $10–$200. You’ll also need API keys for services like Firecrawl, HubSpot, and Google Cloud, which have their own pricing. For a solo founder using it moderately, expect $...\n","siteName":""}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1776249881630}}
{"type":"message","id":"212fc048","parentId":"fe04d723","timestamp":"2026-04-15T10:44:41.865Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_81ehnd55snku_2","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"browser-use agent price scraping tutorial 2025\",\n  \"provider\": \"miaoda\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"GitHub - gokborayilmaz/browseruse-price-tracker-agent: BrowserUse-Price-Tracker-Agent is a powerful AI-powered price tracker that scrapes multiple e-commerce websites for product prices using BrowserU\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/gokborayilmaz/browseruse-price-tracker-agent\",\n      \"description\": \"This agent displays the best deals in a user...\\nInstall <beginning of the code>browser-use<end of the code> and <beginning of the code>playwright<end of the code>\\nBrowserUse requires Playwright for web scraping capabilities. Run the following commands:\\npip install browser-use\\nplaywright install\\nRunning the Application\\nStart the FastAPI Server\\nupsonicai:app --reload\\nOpen the UI\\nGo to http://127.0.\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Top 10 Browser Agents for Web Scraping: Full Guide 2025\",\n      \"url\": \"https://o-mega.ai/articles/top-10-browser-agents-for-web-scraping-full-guide-2025\",\n      \"description\": \"ai )), Axiom Pro at $50/month increases that (and likely allows more complex bots or faster runs), and higher plans like Pro Max (~$150/month) and Ultimate (~$250/month) offer even more hours and features like multiple bots running in parallel, higher cloud execution limits, etc. ((nocodementor.io)) ((jimcarter.me )). Essentially, the pricing is based on how much you want to automate per month and what advanced features...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Browserbase & Web Scraping AI: The 99X Trending Tool That's Changing How Agents Extract Data (November 2025)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.trendflash.net/posts/browserbase-web-scraping-ai-the-99x-trending-tool-thats-changing-how-agents-extract-data-november-2025\",\n      \"description\": \"AI Tools & Apps\\nBrowserbase & Web Scraping AI: The 99X Trending Tool That's Changing How Agents Extract Data (November 2025)\\nBrowserbase is exploding as the go-to cloud browser infrastructure for AI agents. This comprehensive guide covers what it does, real-world use cases, pricing comparisons, step-by-step tutorials with code, and how SaaS agencies are charging $5,000+ monthly for custom web scraping solutions powered by Browserbase....\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"用BrowserUse抓取网页数据 - 汇智网\",\n      \"url\": \"http://www.hubwiz.com/blog/scrape-web-pages-with-browseruse/\",\n      \"description\": \"3、使用BrowserUse开始爬取\\n要开始使用BrowserUse进行网络爬取，您需要以下几样东西：\\nPython：Python是编写脚本所使用的编程语言。您可以从官方网站下载并安装Python。\\nBrowserUse：您需要安装BrowserUse，可以通过pip或Poetry完成。\\nPlaywright：BrowserUse依赖于Playwright，这是一个用于自动化浏览器的库。您需要安装Playwright并设置它来运行您的脚本。\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"浏览器使用 | Scrapeless 爬虫浏览器\",\n      \"url\": \"https://docs.scrapeless.com/zh/scraping-browser/integrations/browser-use/\",\n      \"description\": \"你的 <beginning of the code>.env<end of the code> 文件中也需要 <beginning of the code>OPENAI_API_KEY<end of the code> 环境变量。\\nOPENAI_API_KEY=your-openai-api-key\\nSCRAPELESS_API_KEY=your-scrapeless-api-key\\n运行你的脚本\\n运行你的脚本：\\npython run main.py\\n你应该会看到你的 Scrapeless 会话在 Scrapeless 仪表板 中启动。\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"How to scrape prices from websites with Python\",\n      \"url\": \"https://blog.apify.com/price-scraping-python/\",\n      \"description\": \"This step-by-step tutorial will help you scrape a website using Python. We'll extract pricing data from Ebay.com in this case, but the script is applicable to most e-commerce sites. We'll guide you from setup to deployment on Apify.\\nGuide for scraping prices from websites\\nTo build this scraper, we’ll be using both <beginning of the code>selenium<end of the code> and <beginning of the code>beautifulsoup<end of the code>...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"How to Best Deploy Scrapeless Browser and Browser Use?\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.scrapeless.com/en/blog/browser-use-with-scraping-browser\",\n      \"description\": \"Then copy and set the <beginning of the code>SCRAPELESS_API_KEY<end of the code> environment variables in your .env file.\\nTo enable AI features in Browser-Use, you need a valid API key from an external AI provider. In this example, we will use OpenAI. If you haven't generated an API key yet, follow OpenAI's official guide to create one.\\nThe <beginning of the code>OPENAI_API_KEYenvironment<end...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"How to Build a Browser Use Agent with DeepSeek\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/websites-apps/how-to-build-a-browser-use-agent-with-deepseek/\",\n      \"description\": \"Here are the steps on how to create a powerful browser automation agent using DeepSeek, step-by-step, to automate tasks like scraping, testing, and form filling with ease\\nStep 1: Set Up Your Environment\\nInstall Python and Selenium as listed in prerequisites.\\nget(\\\"https://example-news-site.com\\\")\\n\\n# Use DeepSeek to locate headlines (AI identifies elements)\\nheadlines = deepseek.find_elements(driver, element_type=\\\"headline\\\")\\n\\n# Extract and print...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"User agent web scraping\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.acciyo.com/user-agent-web-scraping/\",\n      \"description\": \"Online Databases: Websites like <beginning of the code>useragentstring.com<end of the code> or <beginning of the code>whatismybrowser.com/guides/the-user-agent<end of the code> provide extensive lists of User-Agents for various browsers, operating systems, and devices.\\nPython Libraries: Libraries like <beginning of the code>fake_useragent<end of the code> for Python can generate random, realistic User-Agents, which...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"How to Make an AI Agent Web Scraper (Beginner-Friendly Tutorial)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.capsolver.com/blog/webscraping/make-ai-agent\",\n      \"description\": \"Tools: Proxy rotators and high-performance CAPTCHA solving services like CapSolver.\\nStep-by-Step Tutorial: Building Your First...\\nStep 1: Set Up Your Environment\\nStart by creating a new project directory and installing the necessary libraries. We recommend using a virtual environment to manage dependencies.\\n# Create a new directory\\nmkdir ai-scraper-agent\\ncd ai-scraper-agent\\n\\n# Install core libraries\\npip install langchain selenium\\nStep 2: Define the Agent's Tools\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"query":"browser-use agent price scraping tutorial 2025","provider":"miaoda","count":10,"results":[{"title":"GitHub - gokborayilmaz/browseruse-price-tracker-agent: BrowserUse-Price-Tracker-Agent is a powerful AI-powered price tracker that scrapes multiple e-commerce websites for product prices using BrowserU","url":"https://github.com/gokborayilmaz/browseruse-price-tracker-agent","description":"This agent displays the best deals in a user...\nInstall <beginning of the code>browser-use<end of the code> and <beginning of the code>playwright<end of the code>\nBrowserUse requires Playwright for web scraping capabilities. Run the following commands:\npip install browser-use\nplaywright install\nRunning the Application\nStart the FastAPI Server\nupsonicai:app --reload\nOpen the UI\nGo to http://127.0.","siteName":""},{"title":"Top 10 Browser Agents for Web Scraping: Full Guide 2025","url":"https://o-mega.ai/articles/top-10-browser-agents-for-web-scraping-full-guide-2025","description":"ai )), Axiom Pro at $50/month increases that (and likely allows more complex bots or faster runs), and higher plans like Pro Max (~$150/month) and Ultimate (~$250/month) offer even more hours and features like multiple bots running in parallel, higher cloud execution limits, etc. ((nocodementor.io)) ((jimcarter.me )). Essentially, the pricing is based on how much you want to automate per month and what advanced features...\n","siteName":""},{"title":"Browserbase & Web Scraping AI: The 99X Trending Tool That's Changing How Agents Extract Data (November 2025)","url":"https://www.trendflash.net/posts/browserbase-web-scraping-ai-the-99x-trending-tool-thats-changing-how-agents-extract-data-november-2025","description":"AI Tools & Apps\nBrowserbase & Web Scraping AI: The 99X Trending Tool That's Changing How Agents Extract Data (November 2025)\nBrowserbase is exploding as the go-to cloud browser infrastructure for AI agents. This comprehensive guide covers what it does, real-world use cases, pricing comparisons, step-by-step tutorials with code, and how SaaS agencies are charging $5,000+ monthly for custom web scraping solutions powered by Browserbase....\n","siteName":""},{"title":"用BrowserUse抓取网页数据 - 汇智网","url":"http://www.hubwiz.com/blog/scrape-web-pages-with-browseruse/","description":"3、使用BrowserUse开始爬取\n要开始使用BrowserUse进行网络爬取，您需要以下几样东西：\nPython：Python是编写脚本所使用的编程语言。您可以从官方网站下载并安装Python。\nBrowserUse：您需要安装BrowserUse，可以通过pip或Poetry完成。\nPlaywright：BrowserUse依赖于Playwright，这是一个用于自动化浏览器的库。您需要安装Playwright并设置它来运行您的脚本。\n","siteName":""},{"title":"浏览器使用 | Scrapeless 爬虫浏览器","url":"https://docs.scrapeless.com/zh/scraping-browser/integrations/browser-use/","description":"你的 <beginning of the code>.env<end of the code> 文件中也需要 <beginning of the code>OPENAI_API_KEY<end of the code> 环境变量。\nOPENAI_API_KEY=your-openai-api-key\nSCRAPELESS_API_KEY=your-scrapeless-api-key\n运行你的脚本\n运行你的脚本：\npython run main.py\n你应该会看到你的 Scrapeless 会话在 Scrapeless 仪表板 中启动。\n","siteName":""},{"title":"How to scrape prices from websites with Python","url":"https://blog.apify.com/price-scraping-python/","description":"This step-by-step tutorial will help you scrape a website using Python. We'll extract pricing data from Ebay.com in this case, but the script is applicable to most e-commerce sites. We'll guide you from setup to deployment on Apify.\nGuide for scraping prices from websites\nTo build this scraper, we’ll be using both <beginning of the code>selenium<end of the code> and <beginning of the code>beautifulsoup<end of the code>...\n","siteName":""},{"title":"How to Best Deploy Scrapeless Browser and Browser Use?","url":"https://www.scrapeless.com/en/blog/browser-use-with-scraping-browser","description":"Then copy and set the <beginning of the code>SCRAPELESS_API_KEY<end of the code> environment variables in your .env file.\nTo enable AI features in Browser-Use, you need a valid API key from an external AI provider. In this example, we will use OpenAI. If you haven't generated an API key yet, follow OpenAI's official guide to create one.\nThe <beginning of the code>OPENAI_API_KEYenvironment<end...\n","siteName":""},{"title":"How to Build a Browser Use Agent with DeepSeek","url":"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/websites-apps/how-to-build-a-browser-use-agent-with-deepseek/","description":"Here are the steps on how to create a powerful browser automation agent using DeepSeek, step-by-step, to automate tasks like scraping, testing, and form filling with ease\nStep 1: Set Up Your Environment\nInstall Python and Selenium as listed in prerequisites.\nget(\"https://example-news-site.com\")\n\n# Use DeepSeek to locate headlines (AI identifies elements)\nheadlines = deepseek.find_elements(driver, element_type=\"headline\")\n\n# Extract and print...\n","siteName":""},{"title":"User agent web scraping","url":"https://www.acciyo.com/user-agent-web-scraping/","description":"Online Databases: Websites like <beginning of the code>useragentstring.com<end of the code> or <beginning of the code>whatismybrowser.com/guides/the-user-agent<end of the code> provide extensive lists of User-Agents for various browsers, operating systems, and devices.\nPython Libraries: Libraries like <beginning of the code>fake_useragent<end of the code> for Python can generate random, realistic User-Agents, which...\n","siteName":""},{"title":"How to Make an AI Agent Web Scraper (Beginner-Friendly Tutorial)","url":"https://www.capsolver.com/blog/webscraping/make-ai-agent","description":"Tools: Proxy rotators and high-performance CAPTCHA solving services like CapSolver.\nStep-by-Step Tutorial: Building Your First...\nStep 1: Set Up Your Environment\nStart by creating a new project directory and installing the necessary libraries. We recommend using a virtual environment to manage dependencies.\n# Create a new directory\nmkdir ai-scraper-agent\ncd ai-scraper-agent\n\n# Install core libraries\npip install langchain selenium\nStep 2: Define the Agent's Tools\n","siteName":""}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1776249881817}}
{"type":"message","id":"ce6aeb42","parentId":"212fc048","timestamp":"2026-04-15T10:44:48.660Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I found some very promising leads! Let me summarize what I found:\n\n1. **OpenClaw Skill - price-monitor**: A skill specifically for OpenClaw that monitors price drops on e-commerce platforms\n2. **Browser-use + Playwright**: A Python library that lets AI agents scrape prices from websites\n3. **Apify**: Has various scrapers including for e-commerce\n4. **Firecrawl**: Has a free tier (500 credits/month) for web scraping\n\nLet me check if there's a clawhub skill for price monitoring that I can install, and also look into browser-use."},{"type":"text","text":"找到了！让我进一步研究这些工具：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_5xow5bbjnnpm_1","name":"web_crawl","arguments":{"url":"https://clawhub.ai/Michael-laffin/price-tracker"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_5xow5bbjnnpm_2","name":"web_crawl","arguments":{"url":"https://www.toolify.ai/openclaw-skills/price-monitor-19693"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"minimax-token-plan","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1776249881868,"responseId":"062e9f191453cba2dd61a2d5fb146708"}}
{"type":"message","id":"9247e2e6","parentId":"ce6aeb42","timestamp":"2026-04-15T10:44:55.654Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_5xow5bbjnnpm_1","toolName":"web_crawl","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"url\": \"https://clawhub.ai/Michael-laffin/price-tracker\",\n  \"content\": \"# Price Tracker\\n\\nv1.0.0\\n\\nMonitor product prices across Amazon, eBay, Walmart, and Best Buy to identify arbitrage opportunities and profit margins. Use when finding products to flip, monitoring competitor pricing, tracking price history, identifying arbitrage opportunities, or setting automated price alerts.\\n\\n⭐ 6·\\n\\n3.4k·17 current·18 all-time\\n\\nby\\n\\nMIT-0\\n\\n\\n\\nLicenseMIT-0 · Free to use, modify, and redistribute. No attribution required.\\n\\nSecurity Scan\\n\\nVirusTotalVirusTotal\\n\\nBenign\\n\\n\\n\\nOpenClawOpenClaw\\n\\nBenign\\n\\nhigh confidence\\n\\nThe skill's code and runtime instructions are coherent with its stated purpose (price monitoring/arbitrage) and do not request unrelated credentials, external downloads, or system-wide privileges.Details \\n\\nPurpose & Capability\\n\\nName/description match the included scripts: search/compare/monitor/price-history logic for Amazon/eBay/Walmart/BestBuy. The code uses internal PLATFORMS and mock search functions rather than any unrelated services, and it does not ask for unrelated environment variables or binaries.\\n\\nInstruction Scope\\n\\nSKILL.md instructs running the provided Python scripts and supplying CSV/input parameters. The scripts read CSVs and produce reports/alerts; they do not attempt to read arbitrary system files, probe environment variables, or transmit data to external endpoints. The README clearly marks platform integrations as placeholders for future API integration.\\n\\nInstall Mechanism\\n\\nThere is no install specification or remote download; the skill is delivered as local Python scripts. No extract-from-URL or external installers are present. Running requires a Python runtime only; no extra packages are declared.\\n\\nCredentials\\n\\nThe skill requires no environment variables, credentials, or config paths. This is proportional to the shipped implementation which uses mock data. Note: switching to real platform APIs in production would legitimately require API keys and secrets — those are not present here.\\n\\nPersistence & Privilege\\n\\nalways is false and the skill does not modify other skills or system-wide agent settings. It prints reports and optionally writes output files, which is appropriate for its function.\\n\\nAssessment\\n\\nThe packaged scripts are coherent and use mock data — they do not contact real e-commerce APIs or exfiltrate data. Before using in production: (1) review and implement proper API integrations (Amazon, eBay, Walmart, Best Buy) and store any API keys securely (don’t hardcode them); (2) be aware of each marketplace’s terms of service and rate limits when adding real network calls; (3) validate CSV inputs before bulk runs and run untrusted CSVs in an isolated environment; (4) if you or a contributor add network calls or third-party libraries, re-audit those changes (look for unexpected endpoints, URL shorteners, or downloads). Overall this package appears internally consistent with its stated purpose.\\n\\nLike a lobster shell, security has layers — review code before you run it.\\n\\nlatestvk9721q9j50p5z0nct8f7ryymes80h089\\n\\n### License\\n\\nMIT-0\\n\\nFree to use, modify, and redistribute. No attribution required.\\n\\n**Terms** \\n\\nFilesCompareVersions\\n\\n## SKILL.md\\n\\n# Price Tracker\\n\\n## Overview\\n\\nTrack product prices across multiple e-commerce platforms to identify arbitrage opportunities, profit margins, and optimal buying/selling windows. This skill enables automated price monitoring, historical tracking, and revenue-focused decision making.\\n\\n## Core Capabilities\\n\\n### 1. Product Discovery & Monitoring\\n\\n**Search and Track Products:**\\n\\n- Search products by keyword across Amazon, eBay, Walmart, Best Buy\\n\\n- Add products to monitoring lists\\n\\n- Set target price thresholds\\n\\n- Configure alert frequency (hourly, daily, weekly)\\n\\n**Example Request:**  \\\"Monitor iPhone 15 Pro prices across Amazon and eBay. Alert me if the price drops below \\\\$800 or if eBay listing is \\\\$150+ cheaper than Amazon.\\\"\\n\\n### 2. Arbitrage Analysis\\n\\n**Cross-Platform Comparison:**\\n\\n- Compare identical product prices across platforms\\n\\n- Calculate profit margins after fees and shipping\\n\\n- Identify flip-worthy opportunities (20%+ margin after costs)\\n\\n- Factor in platform fees, shipping costs, and taxes\\n\\n**Fee Structure Reference:**\\n\\n- Amazon: \\\\~15% referral fee\\n\\n- eBay: \\\\~13% final value fee + listing fees\\n\\n- Walmart: \\\\~8-15% referral fee\\n\\n**Example Request:**  \\\"Find Nintendo Switch bundles where eBay price is 20%+ higher than Amazon, accounting for all fees and shipping costs.\\\"\\n\\n### 3. Historical Price Tracking\\n\\n**Price History:**\\n\\n- Track price changes over time (30, 60, 90 days)\\n\\n- Identify seasonal pricing patterns\\n\\n- Detect price manipulation or flash sales\\n\\n- Export historical data for analysis\\n\\n**Example Request:**  \\\"Show me the price history for AirPods Pro 2 over the last 60 days. Identify the best buying window.\\\"\\n\\n### 4. Automated Alerts\\n\\n**Alert Configuration:**\\n\\n- Price drop alerts (below threshold)\\n\\n- Arbitrage opportunity alerts (margin threshold)\\n\\n- Competitor price alerts (when competitor lowers price)\\n\\n- Bulk product monitoring\\n\\n**Example Request:**  \\\"Set up alerts for all Sony TV models. Alert me if any model drops below \\\\$400 or has 25%+ arbitrage margin.\\\"\\n\\n## Quick Start\\n\\n### Track a Single Product\\n\\n```\\n# Use scripts/track_product.py\\npython3 scripts/track_product.py \\\\\\n --product \\\"Apple iPhone 15 Pro 256GB\\\" \\\\\\n --platforms amazon,ebay \\\\\\n --alert-below 800 \\\\\\n --alert-margin 0.20\\n```\\n### Bulk Monitor Products from CSV\\n\\n```\\n# Use scripts/bulk_monitor.py\\npython3 scripts/bulk_monitor.py \\\\\\n --csv products.csv \\\\\\n --margin-threshold 0.25 \\\\\\n --alert-frequency daily\\n```\\n### Price Comparison Report\\n\\n```\\n# Use scripts/compare_prices.py\\npython3 scripts/compare_prices.py \\\\\\n --keyword \\\"Sony WH-1000XM5\\\" \\\\\\n --platforms amazon,ebay,walmart,bestbuy \\\\\\n --report markdown\\n```\\n## Workflow\\n\\n### Arbitrage Opportunity Discovery\\n\\n1. **Search**  for products in high-demand categories (electronics, gaming, home goods)\\n\\n2. **Compare**  prices across all platforms using `compare_prices.py`\\n\\n3. **Calculate**  net profit after fees/shipping/taxes\\n\\n4. **Filter**  opportunities with 20%+ margin\\n\\n5. **Verify**  product condition and seller reliability\\n\\n6. **Execute**  or set monitoring for price drops\\n\\n### Price Drop Monitoring\\n\\n1. **Identify**  target products (wishlist, seasonally discounted items)\\n\\n2. **Set**  alert thresholds using `track_product.py`\\n\\n3. **Monitor**  historical patterns to predict optimal buy windows\\n\\n4. **Act**  when price drops below threshold\\n\\n5. **Repeat**  for seasonal shopping events (Prime Day, Black Friday)\\n\\n## Scripts\\n\\n### `track_product.py`\\n\\nTrack a single product across platforms with configurable alerts.\\n\\n**Parameters:**\\n\\n- `--product`: Product name/keyword\\n\\n- `--platforms`: Comma-separated platforms (amazon,ebay,walmart,bestbuy)\\n\\n- `--alert-below`: Alert when price drops below this amount\\n\\n- `--alert-margin`: Alert when arbitrage margin exceeds this fraction (e.g., 0.20 = 20%)\\n\\n- `--frequency`: Check frequency (hourly,daily,weekly)\\n\\n- `--output`: Output format (json,csv,markdown)\\n\\n**Example:**\\n\\n```\\npython3 scripts/track_product.py \\\\\\n --product \\\"Samsung Galaxy S24 Ultra 256GB\\\" \\\\\\n --platforms amazon,ebay,walmart \\\\\\n --alert-below 900 \\\\\\n --alert-margin 0.25 \\\\\\n --frequency daily \\\\\\n --output markdown\\n```\\n### `compare_prices.py`\\n\\nCompare prices for a product across all platforms.\\n\\n**Parameters:**\\n\\n- `--keyword`: Product search keyword\\n\\n- `--platforms`: Comma-separated platforms (default: all)\\n\\n- `--report`: Report format (markdown,json,csv)\\n\\n- `--sort-by`: Sort by price, margin, or rating\\n\\n- `--min-rating`: Minimum seller rating\\n\\n**Example:**\\n\\n```\\npython3 scripts/compare_prices.py \\\\\\n --keyword \\\"PlayStation 5 Slim\\\" \\\\\\n --platforms amazon,ebay,walmart,bestbuy \\\\\\n --report markdown \\\\\\n --sort-by margin \\\\\\n --min-rating 4.5\\n```\\n### `bulk_monitor.py`\\n\\nMonitor multiple products from a CSV file.\\n\\n**CSV Format:**\\n\\n```\\nproduct,platforms,alert_below,alert_margin\\n\\\"Apple MacBook Air M3 256GB\\\",amazon,ebay,walmart,899,0.20\\n\\\"Sony PlayStation 5\\\",amazon,ebay,399,0.25\\n\\\"Dyson V15 Detect\\\",amazon,walmart,bestbuy,500,0.18\\n```\\n**Parameters:**\\n\\n- `--csv`: Path to CSV file\\n\\n- `--margin-threshold`: Minimum margin to report\\n\\n- `--alert-frequency`: Frequency of alerts\\n\\n- `--output`: Output file for alerts\\n\\n**Example:**\\n\\n```\\npython3 scripts/bulk_monitor.py \\\\\\n --csv products.csv \\\\\\n --margin-threshold 0.20 \\\\\\n --alert-frequency daily \\\\\\n --output alerts.txt\\n```\\n### `price_history.py`\\n\\nRetrieve and analyze historical price data.\\n\\n**Parameters:**\\n\\n- `--product`: Product name/keyword\\n\\n- `--days`: Number of days of history (default: 30)\\n\\n- `--platform`: Specific platform (optional)\\n\\n- `--output`: Output format (markdown,json,csv)\\n\\n- `--trend-analysis`: Include trend analysis and predictions\\n\\n**Example:**\\n\\n```\\npython3 scripts/price_history.py \\\\\\n --product \\\"AirPods Pro 2\\\" \\\\\\n --days 60 \\\\\\n --trend-analysis \\\\\\n --output markdown\\n```\\n## Best Practices\\n\\n### Arbitrage Profit Calculation\\n\\nAlways calculate net profit:\\n\\n```\\nNet Profit = (Sell Price - Buy Price)\\n - Platform Fees\\n - Shipping Costs\\n - Payment Processing Fees\\n - Taxes\\n```\\n**Recommended minimum margin:**  20-25% to account for:\\n\\n- Unexpected shipping delays\\n\\n- Returns/refunds\\n\\n- Market price fluctuations\\n\\n- Time value of money\\n\\n### Risk Mitigation\\n\\n1. **Verify seller reliability**  - Check ratings and reviews\\n\\n2. **Check product condition**  - New, refurbished, or used\\n\\n3. **Factor in return windows**  - Platforms have different policies\\n\\n4. **Monitor price stability**  - Volatile prices increase risk\\n\\n5. **Stay within limits**  - Don't over-leverage on single opportunities\\n\\n### Seasonal Patterns\\n\\n- **Q4 (Oct-Dec):**  Holiday sales, best for electronics\\n\\n- **January:**  Post-holiday clearance\\n\\n- **Prime Day (July):**  Amazon-specific deals\\n\\n- **Black Friday/Cyber Monday:**  Cross-platform discounts\\n\\n- **Back-to-School (Aug-Sep):**  Laptops, tablets, accessories\\n\\n## Automation Integration\\n\\n### Set Up Cron Jobs for Automated Monitoring\\n\\n```\\n# Check prices every 6 hours\\n0 */6 * * * /path/to/price-tracker/scripts/bulk_monitor.py --csv products.csv --output alerts.txt\\n\\n# Daily arbitrage scan\\n0 9 * * * /path/to/price-tracker/scripts/compare_prices.py --keyword \\\"high-demand-products\\\" --report markdown >> /path/to/reports.txt\\n```\\n### Integration with Notifications\\n\\nCombine with notification systems (email, Discord, Telegram) to receive real-time alerts when opportunities are detected.\\n\\n## Limitations\\n\\n- Platform API rate limits may affect search frequency\\n\\n- Real-time prices may have slight delays\\n\\n- Some platforms restrict scraping (comply with ToS)\\n\\n- Seller inventory changes rapidly\\n\\n**Revenue first. Track smart. Flip fast.**\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n6 total\\n\\nSKILL.md7.6 KBscripts/__init__.py24 Bscripts/bulk_monitor.py4.6 KBscripts/compare_prices.py3.6 KBscripts/price_history.py5.9 KBscripts/track_product.py7.3 KB\\n\\n## Comments\"\n}"}],"details":{"url":"https://clawhub.ai/Michael-laffin/price-tracker","content":"# Price Tracker\n\nv1.0.0\n\nMonitor product prices across Amazon, eBay, Walmart, and Best Buy to identify arbitrage opportunities and profit margins. Use when finding products to flip, monitoring competitor pricing, tracking price history, identifying arbitrage opportunities, or setting automated price alerts.\n\n⭐ 6·\n\n3.4k·17 current·18 all-time\n\nby\n\nMIT-0\n\n\n\nLicenseMIT-0 · Free to use, modify, and redistribute. No attribution required.\n\nSecurity Scan\n\nVirusTotalVirusTotal\n\nBenign\n\n\n\nOpenClawOpenClaw\n\nBenign\n\nhigh confidence\n\nThe skill's code and runtime instructions are coherent with its stated purpose (price monitoring/arbitrage) and do not request unrelated credentials, external downloads, or system-wide privileges.Details \n\nPurpose & Capability\n\nName/description match the included scripts: search/compare/monitor/price-history logic for Amazon/eBay/Walmart/BestBuy. The code uses internal PLATFORMS and mock search functions rather than any unrelated services, and it does not ask for unrelated environment variables or binaries.\n\nInstruction Scope\n\nSKILL.md instructs running the provided Python scripts and supplying CSV/input parameters. The scripts read CSVs and produce reports/alerts; they do not attempt to read arbitrary system files, probe environment variables, or transmit data to external endpoints. The README clearly marks platform integrations as placeholders for future API integration.\n\nInstall Mechanism\n\nThere is no install specification or remote download; the skill is delivered as local Python scripts. No extract-from-URL or external installers are present. Running requires a Python runtime only; no extra packages are declared.\n\nCredentials\n\nThe skill requires no environment variables, credentials, or config paths. This is proportional to the shipped implementation which uses mock data. Note: switching to real platform APIs in production would legitimately require API keys and secrets — those are not present here.\n\nPersistence & Privilege\n\nalways is false and the skill does not modify other skills or system-wide agent settings. It prints reports and optionally writes output files, which is appropriate for its function.\n\nAssessment\n\nThe packaged scripts are coherent and use mock data — they do not contact real e-commerce APIs or exfiltrate data. Before using in production: (1) review and implement proper API integrations (Amazon, eBay, Walmart, Best Buy) and store any API keys securely (don’t hardcode them); (2) be aware of each marketplace’s terms of service and rate limits when adding real network calls; (3) validate CSV inputs before bulk runs and run untrusted CSVs in an isolated environment; (4) if you or a contributor add network calls or third-party libraries, re-audit those changes (look for unexpected endpoints, URL shorteners, or downloads). Overall this package appears internally consistent with its stated purpose.\n\nLike a lobster shell, security has layers — review code before you run it.\n\nlatestvk9721q9j50p5z0nct8f7ryymes80h089\n\n### License\n\nMIT-0\n\nFree to use, modify, and redistribute. No attribution required.\n\n**Terms** \n\nFilesCompareVersions\n\n## SKILL.md\n\n# Price Tracker\n\n## Overview\n\nTrack product prices across multiple e-commerce platforms to identify arbitrage opportunities, profit margins, and optimal buying/selling windows. This skill enables automated price monitoring, historical tracking, and revenue-focused decision making.\n\n## Core Capabilities\n\n### 1. Product Discovery & Monitoring\n\n**Search and Track Products:**\n\n- Search products by keyword across Amazon, eBay, Walmart, Best Buy\n\n- Add products to monitoring lists\n\n- Set target price thresholds\n\n- Configure alert frequency (hourly, daily, weekly)\n\n**Example Request:**  \"Monitor iPhone 15 Pro prices across Amazon and eBay. Alert me if the price drops below \\$800 or if eBay listing is \\$150+ cheaper than Amazon.\"\n\n### 2. Arbitrage Analysis\n\n**Cross-Platform Comparison:**\n\n- Compare identical product prices across platforms\n\n- Calculate profit margins after fees and shipping\n\n- Identify flip-worthy opportunities (20%+ margin after costs)\n\n- Factor in platform fees, shipping costs, and taxes\n\n**Fee Structure Reference:**\n\n- Amazon: \\~15% referral fee\n\n- eBay: \\~13% final value fee + listing fees\n\n- Walmart: \\~8-15% referral fee\n\n**Example Request:**  \"Find Nintendo Switch bundles where eBay price is 20%+ higher than Amazon, accounting for all fees and shipping costs.\"\n\n### 3. Historical Price Tracking\n\n**Price History:**\n\n- Track price changes over time (30, 60, 90 days)\n\n- Identify seasonal pricing patterns\n\n- Detect price manipulation or flash sales\n\n- Export historical data for analysis\n\n**Example Request:**  \"Show me the price history for AirPods Pro 2 over the last 60 days. Identify the best buying window.\"\n\n### 4. Automated Alerts\n\n**Alert Configuration:**\n\n- Price drop alerts (below threshold)\n\n- Arbitrage opportunity alerts (margin threshold)\n\n- Competitor price alerts (when competitor lowers price)\n\n- Bulk product monitoring\n\n**Example Request:**  \"Set up alerts for all Sony TV models. Alert me if any model drops below \\$400 or has 25%+ arbitrage margin.\"\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### Track a Single Product\n\n```\n# Use scripts/track_product.py\npython3 scripts/track_product.py \\\n --product \"Apple iPhone 15 Pro 256GB\" \\\n --platforms amazon,ebay \\\n --alert-below 800 \\\n --alert-margin 0.20\n```\n### Bulk Monitor Products from CSV\n\n```\n# Use scripts/bulk_monitor.py\npython3 scripts/bulk_monitor.py \\\n --csv products.csv \\\n --margin-threshold 0.25 \\\n --alert-frequency daily\n```\n### Price Comparison Report\n\n```\n# Use scripts/compare_prices.py\npython3 scripts/compare_prices.py \\\n --keyword \"Sony WH-1000XM5\" \\\n --platforms amazon,ebay,walmart,bestbuy \\\n --report markdown\n```\n## Workflow\n\n### Arbitrage Opportunity Discovery\n\n1. **Search**  for products in high-demand categories (electronics, gaming, home goods)\n\n2. **Compare**  prices across all platforms using `compare_prices.py`\n\n3. **Calculate**  net profit after fees/shipping/taxes\n\n4. **Filter**  opportunities with 20%+ margin\n\n5. **Verify**  product condition and seller reliability\n\n6. **Execute**  or set monitoring for price drops\n\n### Price Drop Monitoring\n\n1. **Identify**  target products (wishlist, seasonally discounted items)\n\n2. **Set**  alert thresholds using `track_product.py`\n\n3. **Monitor**  historical patterns to predict optimal buy windows\n\n4. **Act**  when price drops below threshold\n\n5. **Repeat**  for seasonal shopping events (Prime Day, Black Friday)\n\n## Scripts\n\n### `track_product.py`\n\nTrack a single product across platforms with configurable alerts.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\n- `--product`: Product name/keyword\n\n- `--platforms`: Comma-separated platforms (amazon,ebay,walmart,bestbuy)\n\n- `--alert-below`: Alert when price drops below this amount\n\n- `--alert-margin`: Alert when arbitrage margin exceeds this fraction (e.g., 0.20 = 20%)\n\n- `--frequency`: Check frequency (hourly,daily,weekly)\n\n- `--output`: Output format (json,csv,markdown)\n\n**Example:**\n\n```\npython3 scripts/track_product.py \\\n --product \"Samsung Galaxy S24 Ultra 256GB\" \\\n --platforms amazon,ebay,walmart \\\n --alert-below 900 \\\n --alert-margin 0.25 \\\n --frequency daily \\\n --output markdown\n```\n### `compare_prices.py`\n\nCompare prices for a product across all platforms.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\n- `--keyword`: Product search keyword\n\n- `--platforms`: Comma-separated platforms (default: all)\n\n- `--report`: Report format (markdown,json,csv)\n\n- `--sort-by`: Sort by price, margin, or rating\n\n- `--min-rating`: Minimum seller rating\n\n**Example:**\n\n```\npython3 scripts/compare_prices.py \\\n --keyword \"PlayStation 5 Slim\" \\\n --platforms amazon,ebay,walmart,bestbuy \\\n --report markdown \\\n --sort-by margin \\\n --min-rating 4.5\n```\n### `bulk_monitor.py`\n\nMonitor multiple products from a CSV file.\n\n**CSV Format:**\n\n```\nproduct,platforms,alert_below,alert_margin\n\"Apple MacBook Air M3 256GB\",amazon,ebay,walmart,899,0.20\n\"Sony PlayStation 5\",amazon,ebay,399,0.25\n\"Dyson V15 Detect\",amazon,walmart,bestbuy,500,0.18\n```\n**Parameters:**\n\n- `--csv`: Path to CSV file\n\n- `--margin-threshold`: Minimum margin to report\n\n- `--alert-frequency`: Frequency of alerts\n\n- `--output`: Output file for alerts\n\n**Example:**\n\n```\npython3 scripts/bulk_monitor.py \\\n --csv products.csv \\\n --margin-threshold 0.20 \\\n --alert-frequency daily \\\n --output alerts.txt\n```\n### `price_history.py`\n\nRetrieve and analyze historical price data.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\n- `--product`: Product name/keyword\n\n- `--days`: Number of days of history (default: 30)\n\n- `--platform`: Specific platform (optional)\n\n- `--output`: Output format (markdown,json,csv)\n\n- `--trend-analysis`: Include trend analysis and predictions\n\n**Example:**\n\n```\npython3 scripts/price_history.py \\\n --product \"AirPods Pro 2\" \\\n --days 60 \\\n --trend-analysis \\\n --output markdown\n```\n## Best Practices\n\n### Arbitrage Profit Calculation\n\nAlways calculate net profit:\n\n```\nNet Profit = (Sell Price - Buy Price)\n - Platform Fees\n - Shipping Costs\n - Payment Processing Fees\n - Taxes\n```\n**Recommended minimum margin:**  20-25% to account for:\n\n- Unexpected shipping delays\n\n- Returns/refunds\n\n- Market price fluctuations\n\n- Time value of money\n\n### Risk Mitigation\n\n1. **Verify seller reliability**  - Check ratings and reviews\n\n2. **Check product condition**  - New, refurbished, or used\n\n3. **Factor in return windows**  - Platforms have different policies\n\n4. **Monitor price stability**  - Volatile prices increase risk\n\n5. **Stay within limits**  - Don't over-leverage on single opportunities\n\n### Seasonal Patterns\n\n- **Q4 (Oct-Dec):**  Holiday sales, best for electronics\n\n- **January:**  Post-holiday clearance\n\n- **Prime Day (July):**  Amazon-specific deals\n\n- **Black Friday/Cyber Monday:**  Cross-platform discounts\n\n- **Back-to-School (Aug-Sep):**  Laptops, tablets, accessories\n\n## Automation Integration\n\n### Set Up Cron Jobs for Automated Monitoring\n\n```\n# Check prices every 6 hours\n0 */6 * * * /path/to/price-tracker/scripts/bulk_monitor.py --csv products.csv --output alerts.txt\n\n# Daily arbitrage scan\n0 9 * * * /path/to/price-tracker/scripts/compare_prices.py --keyword \"high-demand-products\" --report markdown >> /path/to/reports.txt\n```\n### Integration with Notifications\n\nCombine with notification systems (email, Discord, Telegram) to receive real-time alerts when opportunities are detected.\n\n## Limitations\n\n- Platform API rate limits may affect search frequency\n\n- Real-time prices may have slight delays\n\n- Some platforms restrict scraping (comply with ToS)\n\n- Seller inventory changes rapidly\n\n**Revenue first. Track smart. Flip fast.**\n\n### Files\n\n6 total\n\nSKILL.md7.6 KBscripts/__init__.py24 Bscripts/bulk_monitor.py4.6 KBscripts/compare_prices.py3.6 KBscripts/price_history.py5.9 KBscripts/track_product.py7.3 KB\n\n## Comments"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1776249895607}}
{"type":"message","id":"ff3d5e7c","parentId":"9247e2e6","timestamp":"2026-04-15T10:44:55.702Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_5xow5bbjnnpm_2","toolName":"web_crawl","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"url\": \"https://www.toolify.ai/openclaw-skills/price-monitor-19693\",\n  \"content\": \"price-monitor for Openclaw\\nA robust browser automation tool for monitoring e-commerce price changes, stock availability, and content updates with historical logging and alerts.\\nyinanping-cpu\\nv1.0.0\\nMar 7, 2026\\n0\\n171\\n5\\nInformation\\nSkill.md\\nInstall & Download\\n1. ClawHub CLI\\nThe fastest way to install a skill directly from the registry.\\nnpx clawhub@latest install price-monitor\\n2. Manual Installation\\nCopy the skill folder to one of these locations\\nGlobal\\n~/.openclaw/skills/\\nWorkspace\\n<project>/skills/\\nPriority: Workspace > Local > Bundled\\n3. Prompt Installation\\nCopy this prompt to OpenClaw to install it automatically.\\nHelp me install price-monitor using Clawhub. If Clawhub is not installed, install it first (npm i -g clawhub).\\nWhat is price-monitor?\\nThe price-monitor skill provides developers with a streamlined way to track dynamic web content through browser automation. By leveraging agent-browser capabilities, it allows for the extraction of specific data points like price tags and inventory status from any website. As part of the wider Openclaw Skills ecosystem, this tool is designed for reliability, supporting headless browser operations and persistent data logging for long-term analysis.\\nThis skill is particularly valuable for building market intelligence tools or personal shopping assistants. It eliminates the need for manual site checks by providing a programmable framework to watch for specific triggers, such as price drops or restock events, ensuring you never miss a critical change on the web.\\nprice-monitor Use Cases\\nMonitoring product price drops on major e-commerce platforms like Amazon or Best Buy.\\nReceiving instant notifications when high-demand, out-of-stock items become available.\\nBuilding a comprehensive historical price database for market analysis and trend forecasting.\\nTracking competitor website changes, promotional updates, or new product launches automatically.\\nHow price-monitor Works\\nThe skill utilizes agent-browser to navigate to a target URL defined in your configuration.\\nIt captures a DOM snapshot to identify specific price or inventory elements via CSS selectors.\\nA Python script extracts the current text or value from the identified elements.\\nThe system compares the new data against the previous entry in the history log to detect changes.\\nIf a change exceeds a defined threshold, the skill triggers an alert via Discord, email, or terminal output.\\nprice-monitor Setup\\nTo get started with this skill, you can manually check a product using the following commands:\\nagent-browser open \\\"https://example.com/product/123\\\"\\nagent-browser snapshot -i\\nagent-browser get text @e1\\nFor automated bulk monitoring, prepare a products.csv file and run the provided monitoring script within your Openclaw Skills environment:\\npython scripts/monitor_prices.py products.csv\\nprice-monitor Data Schema & Taxonomy\\nThe skill organizes tracking data primarily in CSV format for high portability. This allows for easy integration with data analysis tools or spreadsheets.\\nField Description\\nurl The target product webpage\\nselector The CSS selector used to find the data element\\nname Human-readable product or item name\\ntimestamp The exact date and time the check was performed\\nprice The extracted numerical value or stock status\\nprice-monitor Advanced Features\\nScheduled automation via Cron jobs to enable persistent monitoring without manual intervention.\\nMulti-channel notification support including Discord webhooks and SMTP email alerts.\\nConfigurable alert thresholds to filter out minor price fluctuations and reduce notification noise.\\nHeadless browser support for running stealthy Openclaw Skills workflows in the background of any server or local machine.\\nSKILL.md\\nname: price-monitor\\ndescription: Monitor website prices, inventory, and content changes using browser automation. Use when tracking e-commerce prices, competitor monitoring, stock alerts, or any web content change detection. Supports scheduled checks, price history logging, and alert notifications.\\nPrice Monitor\\nOverview\\nAutomated price and content monitoring skill using agent-browser. Tracks price changes, stock availability, and content updates on any website with configurable alerts and history logging.\\nQuick Start\\n# Monitor a product price\\nagent-browser open \\\"https://example.com/product/123\\\"\\nagent-browser snapshot -i\\nagent-browser get text @e1  # Get price element\\nCore Workflows\\n1. Single Product Price Check\\nUse case: Check current price of a specific product\\n# Navigate to product page\\nagent-browser open \\\"<product-url>\\\"\\n\\n# Get page snapshot to find price element\\nagent-browser snapshot -i\\n\\n# Extract price (use appropriate ref from snapshot)\\nagent-browser get text @e1\\n\\n# Optional: Save to history log\\necho \\\"$(date), $(price)\\\" >> price-history.csv\\n2. Multi-Product Monitoring\\nUse case: Track prices across multiple products/competitors\\nCreate a products.csv with URLs and price selectors:\\nurl,selector,name\\nhttps://site-a.com/product1,.price-tag,Product A\\nhttps://site-b.com/item2,#price,Product B\\nRun monitoring script:\\npython scripts/monitor_prices.py products.csv\\n3. Stock/Inventory Alerts\\nUse case: Get notified when out-of-stock items become available\\nagent-browser open \\\"<product-url>\\\"\\nagent-browser snapshot -i\\nagent-browser get text @e1  # Check for \\\"In Stock\\\" or \\\"Out of Stock\\\"\\n4. Price History Tracking\\nUse case: Build historical price data for analysis\\nScript automatically logs:\\nTimestamp\\nProduct name/URL\\nCurrent price\\nStock status\\nOutput: price-history.csv or JSON format\\nScripts\\nmonitor_prices.py\\nMain monitoring script that:\\nReads product list from CSV\\nNavigates to each URL\\nExtracts price using CSS selector\\nLogs results with timestamp\\nDetects price changes\\nOptional: Send alerts on significant changes\\nUsage:\\npython scripts/monitor_prices.py products.csv [--alert-threshold 10]\\nArguments:\\nproducts.csv - Product list with URLs and selectors\\n--alert-threshold - Percentage change to trigger alert (default: 10%)\\nConfiguration\\nProduct List Format (CSV)\\nurl,selector,name,min_price,max_price\\nhttps://amazon.com/dp/B08N5WRWNW,.a-price-whole,Sony Headphones,50,150\\nhttps://bestbuy.com/site/12345,.priceView-hero-price,TV,200,500\\nAlert Options\\nEmail alerts - Configure SMTP settings\\nDiscord webhook - Post to Discord channel\\nFile logging - Append to CSV/JSON\\nConsole output - Print changes to terminal\\nBest Practices\\nRate limiting - Add delays between requests (30s+ recommended)\\nError handling - Handle page load failures gracefully\\nSelector stability - Use stable CSS selectors, avoid dynamic classes\\nHeadless mode - Run browser in headless mode for automation\\nSchedule wisely - Check prices during business hours for accuracy\\nExample: Daily Price Check Cron\\n# Run every day at 9 AM\\n0 9 * * * cd /path/to/skill && python scripts/monitor_prices.py products.csv\\nTroubleshooting\\nElement not found : Re-run snapshot to get updated refs\\nPrice format issues : Adjust selector or parse with regex\\nPage load timeout : Increase timeout or add wait condition\\nBlocked by site : Add delays, rotate user agents, or use residential proxy\\nWeb Collection\\nAPI Integrator\\nCategories\\nBrowser Automation\\nE-commerce & Shopping\\n\"\n}"}],"details":{"url":"https://www.toolify.ai/openclaw-skills/price-monitor-19693","content":"price-monitor for Openclaw\nA robust browser automation tool for monitoring e-commerce price changes, stock availability, and content updates with historical logging and alerts.\nyinanping-cpu\nv1.0.0\nMar 7, 2026\n0\n171\n5\nInformation\nSkill.md\nInstall & Download\n1. ClawHub CLI\nThe fastest way to install a skill directly from the registry.\nnpx clawhub@latest install price-monitor\n2. Manual Installation\nCopy the skill folder to one of these locations\nGlobal\n~/.openclaw/skills/\nWorkspace\n<project>/skills/\nPriority: Workspace > Local > Bundled\n3. Prompt Installation\nCopy this prompt to OpenClaw to install it automatically.\nHelp me install price-monitor using Clawhub. If Clawhub is not installed, install it first (npm i -g clawhub).\nWhat is price-monitor?\nThe price-monitor skill provides developers with a streamlined way to track dynamic web content through browser automation. By leveraging agent-browser capabilities, it allows for the extraction of specific data points like price tags and inventory status from any website. As part of the wider Openclaw Skills ecosystem, this tool is designed for reliability, supporting headless browser operations and persistent data logging for long-term analysis.\nThis skill is particularly valuable for building market intelligence tools or personal shopping assistants. It eliminates the need for manual site checks by providing a programmable framework to watch for specific triggers, such as price drops or restock events, ensuring you never miss a critical change on the web.\nprice-monitor Use Cases\nMonitoring product price drops on major e-commerce platforms like Amazon or Best Buy.\nReceiving instant notifications when high-demand, out-of-stock items become available.\nBuilding a comprehensive historical price database for market analysis and trend forecasting.\nTracking competitor website changes, promotional updates, or new product launches automatically.\nHow price-monitor Works\nThe skill utilizes agent-browser to navigate to a target URL defined in your configuration.\nIt captures a DOM snapshot to identify specific price or inventory elements via CSS selectors.\nA Python script extracts the current text or value from the identified elements.\nThe system compares the new data against the previous entry in the history log to detect changes.\nIf a change exceeds a defined threshold, the skill triggers an alert via Discord, email, or terminal output.\nprice-monitor Setup\nTo get started with this skill, you can manually check a product using the following commands:\nagent-browser open \"https://example.com/product/123\"\nagent-browser snapshot -i\nagent-browser get text @e1\nFor automated bulk monitoring, prepare a products.csv file and run the provided monitoring script within your Openclaw Skills environment:\npython scripts/monitor_prices.py products.csv\nprice-monitor Data Schema & Taxonomy\nThe skill organizes tracking data primarily in CSV format for high portability. This allows for easy integration with data analysis tools or spreadsheets.\nField Description\nurl The target product webpage\nselector The CSS selector used to find the data element\nname Human-readable product or item name\ntimestamp The exact date and time the check was performed\nprice The extracted numerical value or stock status\nprice-monitor Advanced Features\nScheduled automation via Cron jobs to enable persistent monitoring without manual intervention.\nMulti-channel notification support including Discord webhooks and SMTP email alerts.\nConfigurable alert thresholds to filter out minor price fluctuations and reduce notification noise.\nHeadless browser support for running stealthy Openclaw Skills workflows in the background of any server or local machine.\nSKILL.md\nname: price-monitor\ndescription: Monitor website prices, inventory, and content changes using browser automation. Use when tracking e-commerce prices, competitor monitoring, stock alerts, or any web content change detection. Supports scheduled checks, price history logging, and alert notifications.\nPrice Monitor\nOverview\nAutomated price and content monitoring skill using agent-browser. Tracks price changes, stock availability, and content updates on any website with configurable alerts and history logging.\nQuick Start\n# Monitor a product price\nagent-browser open \"https://example.com/product/123\"\nagent-browser snapshot -i\nagent-browser get text @e1  # Get price element\nCore Workflows\n1. Single Product Price Check\nUse case: Check current price of a specific product\n# Navigate to product page\nagent-browser open \"<product-url>\"\n\n# Get page snapshot to find price element\nagent-browser snapshot -i\n\n# Extract price (use appropriate ref from snapshot)\nagent-browser get text @e1\n\n# Optional: Save to history log\necho \"$(date), $(price)\" >> price-history.csv\n2. Multi-Product Monitoring\nUse case: Track prices across multiple products/competitors\nCreate a products.csv with URLs and price selectors:\nurl,selector,name\nhttps://site-a.com/product1,.price-tag,Product A\nhttps://site-b.com/item2,#price,Product B\nRun monitoring script:\npython scripts/monitor_prices.py products.csv\n3. Stock/Inventory Alerts\nUse case: Get notified when out-of-stock items become available\nagent-browser open \"<product-url>\"\nagent-browser snapshot -i\nagent-browser get text @e1  # Check for \"In Stock\" or \"Out of Stock\"\n4. Price History Tracking\nUse case: Build historical price data for analysis\nScript automatically logs:\nTimestamp\nProduct name/URL\nCurrent price\nStock status\nOutput: price-history.csv or JSON format\nScripts\nmonitor_prices.py\nMain monitoring script that:\nReads product list from CSV\nNavigates to each URL\nExtracts price using CSS selector\nLogs results with timestamp\nDetects price changes\nOptional: Send alerts on significant changes\nUsage:\npython scripts/monitor_prices.py products.csv [--alert-threshold 10]\nArguments:\nproducts.csv - Product list with URLs and selectors\n--alert-threshold - Percentage change to trigger alert (default: 10%)\nConfiguration\nProduct List Format (CSV)\nurl,selector,name,min_price,max_price\nhttps://amazon.com/dp/B08N5WRWNW,.a-price-whole,Sony Headphones,50,150\nhttps://bestbuy.com/site/12345,.priceView-hero-price,TV,200,500\nAlert Options\nEmail alerts - Configure SMTP settings\nDiscord webhook - Post to Discord channel\nFile logging - Append to CSV/JSON\nConsole output - Print changes to terminal\nBest Practices\nRate limiting - Add delays between requests (30s+ recommended)\nError handling - Handle page load failures gracefully\nSelector stability - Use stable CSS selectors, avoid dynamic classes\nHeadless mode - Run browser in headless mode for automation\nSchedule wisely - Check prices during business hours for accuracy\nExample: Daily Price Check Cron\n# Run every day at 9 AM\n0 9 * * * cd /path/to/skill && python scripts/monitor_prices.py products.csv\nTroubleshooting\nElement not found : Re-run snapshot to get updated refs\nPrice format issues : Adjust selector or parse with regex\nPage load timeout : Increase timeout or add wait condition\nBlocked by site : Add delays, rotate user agents, or use residential proxy\nWeb Collection\nAPI Integrator\nCategories\nBrowser Automation\nE-commerce & Shopping\n"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1776249895654}}
{"type":"message","id":"026d0aa2","parentId":"ff3d5e7c","timestamp":"2026-04-15T10:45:12.813Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! I found two very relevant skills on ClawHub:\n\n1. **Price Tracker** (by Michael Laffin) - MIT-0 license, free to use\n   - Tracks prices across Amazon, eBay, Walmart, Best Buy\n   - Uses mock data currently but has placeholders for real API integration\n   - Scripts: track_product.py, compare_prices.py, bulk_monitor.py, price_history.py\n\n2. **price-monitor** - Uses agent-browser for automation\n   - Monitors e-commerce price changes\n   - Supports headless browser operations\n   - Can use CSV for bulk monitoring\n   - Cron job support\n\nLet me summarize these findings for the user. The key insight is that:\n1. These are real tools available on ClawHub\n2. They use browser automation (Playwright/Puppeteer-based)\n3. Some have free tiers\n4. They can be installed via clawhub CLI\n\nBut the fundamental challenge remains: to get REAL prices, you still need to either:\n- Use official APIs (like Amazon Product API, which requires registration)\n- Scrape websites directly (which 1688 blocks)\n- Use third-party services (like the ones I found that have free tiers)\n\nThe browser-use approach with Playwright could work for sites that don't block automation."},{"type":"text","text":"## 🔍 搜索结果：找到免费的价格检索工具！\n\n### 1️⃣ **Price Tracker** (ClawHub)\n- ⭐ 6个评分 · MIT-0许可证（免费）\n- 支持：Amazon、eBay、Walmart、Best Buy\n- **注意**：目前使用mock数据，需要接入真实API\n\n```\nclawhub install price-tracker\n```\n\n### 2️⃣ **price-monitor** (ClawHub)\n- 使用 `agent-browser` 浏览器自动化\n- 支持定时任务监控 + CSV批量管理\n- 可对接 Discord/SMTP 报警\n\n```\nclawhub install price-monitor\n```\n\n### 3️⃣ **Browser-use + Playwright**\n- AI驱动的价格追踪Agent\n- GitHub: `browseruse-price-tracker-agent`\n- 可以自动导航到电商页面、提取价格\n\n### 4️⃣ **第三方免费API**\n\n| 服务 | 免费额度 | 说明 |\n|------|---------|------|\n| **ScrapingBee** | 1000次/月 | 反爬虫处理 |\n| **Firecrawl** | 500次/月 | AI友好型爬虫 |\n| **XCrawl** | 1000次/首月 | 支持JS渲染 |\n| **Commoditic** (农产品) | 部分免费 | 国际农产品价格 |\n\n---\n\n## 💡 我的建议\n\n**现在最可行的方案**：\n\n```bash\n# 安装 price-monitor skill\nclawhub install price-monitor\n\n# 配置您的目标URL列表（CSV）\n# 运行监控脚本\npython scripts/monitor_prices.py products.csv\n```\n\n**但核心问题不变**：\n- 1688 反爬虫 → 需要用1688官方API\n- 实时价格 → 需要真实数据源\n\n**您想让我现在安装这些skill试试？** 还是先专注于1688账号注册，拿到API Key后再做完整方案？"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"minimax-token-plan","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1776249895706,"responseId":"062e9f2785e90d264eb2a1d3d2bebfb9"}}
