{"type":"message","id":"97b97b18","parentId":"a9f9bf0f","timestamp":"2026-04-15T10:52:36.603Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_ijrmw9sefacj_1","toolName":"web_crawl","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/YutianGe/awesome-openclaw-skills\",\n  \"content\": \"Folders and files\\nName Name Last commit message Last commit date\\nnecatiozmen\\nadd star history\\nd3dd6b9  ·\\n166 Commits\\nCONTRIBUTING.md\\nCONTRIBUTING.md\\nupdate README\\nLICENSE\\nLICENSE\\nRefactor code structure for improved readability and maintainability\\nREADME.md\\nREADME.md\\nadd star history\\nAwesome OpenClaw Skills\\nOpenClaw (previously known as Moltbot, originally Clawdbot... identity crisis included, no extra charge) is a locally-running AI assistant that operates directly on your machine. Skills extend its capabilities, allowing it to interact with external services, automate workflows, and perform specialized tasks. This collection helps you discover and install the right skills for your needs.\\nSkills in this list are sourced from ClawHub  (OpenClaw's public skills registry) and categorized for easier discovery.\\nInstallation\\nClawHub CLI\\nNote: As you probably know, they keep renaming things. This reflects the current official docs. We'll update this when they rename it again.\\nnpx clawhub@latest install <skill-slug>\\nManual Installation\\nCopy the skill folder to one of these locations:\\nLocation Path\\nGlobal~/.openclaw/skills/\\nWorkspace<project>/skills/\\nPriority: Workspace > Local > Bundled\\nAlternative\\nYou can also paste the skill's GitHub repository link directly into your assistant's chat and ask it to use it. The assistant will handle the setup automatically in the background.\\nWhy This List Exists?\\nOpenClaw's public registry (ClawHub) hosts 5,705 community-built skills as of February 7, 2026. This awesome list has 2,868 skills. Here's what we filtered out:\\nFilter Excluded\\nPossibly spam — bulk accounts, bot accounts, test/junk 1,180\\nCrypto / Blockchain / Finance / Trade 672\\nDuplicate / Similar name 492\\nMalicious — identified by security audits published by researchers (excluding VirusTotal) 396\\nNon-English — descriptions not in English 8\\nTotal not taken from OpenClaw's official skill registry 2,748\\nSecurity Notice\\nSkills in this list are curated, not audited. They may be updated, modified, or replaced by their original maintainers at any time after being added here.\\nBefore installing or using any Agent Skill, review potential security risks and validate the source yourself. OpenClaw has a VirusTotal partnership that provides security scanning for skills, visit a skill's page on ClawHub and check the VirusTotal report to see if it's flagged as risky.\\nRecommended tools:\\nSnyk Skill Security Scanner\\nAgent Trust Hub\\nAgent skills can include prompt injections, tool poisoning, hidden malware payloads, or unsafe data handling patterns. Always review the source code before installing and use skills at your own discretion.\\nWant to add a skill? This list only includes skills that are already published in the github.com/openclaw/skills  repository. We do not accept links to personal repos, gists, or any other external source. If your skill isn't in the OpenClaw skills repo yet, publish it there first. See CONTRIBUTING.md for details.\\nIf you believe a skill in this list should be flagged or has a security concern, please open an issue  so we can review it.\\nTable of Contents\\nCoding Agents & IDEs (133) Marketing & Sales  (143) Communication  (132)\\nGit & GitHub (66) Productivity & Tasks  (135) Speech & Transcription  (65)\\nMoltbook (51) AI & LLMs  (287) Smart Home & IoT  (56)\\nWeb & Frontend Development (202) Data & Analytics  (46) Shopping & E-commerce  (51)\\nDevOps & Cloud (212) Finance  (22) Calendar & Scheduling  (50)\\nBrowser & Automation (139) Media & Streaming (80) PDF & Documents  (67)\\nImage & Video Generation (60) Notes & PKM (100) Self-Hosted & Automation  (25)\\nApple Apps & Services (35) iOS & macOS Development  (17) Security & Passwords  (64)\\nSearch & Research (253) Transportation  (76) Gaming (61)\\nClawdbot Tools (120) Personal Development  (56) Agent-to-Agent Protocols  (18)\\nCLI Utilities (129) Health & Fitness  (55)\\nOpenClaw Deployment Stack\\nSetup, hosting, and deployment providers for OpenClaw agents.\\nSponsor spots are reserved for hosting, deployment, and setup providers serving OpenClaw developers & users.\\n📩 For sponsorship inquiries, reach out at necati@voltagent.dev\\nYour product description here — a one-liner about what you offer to OpenClaw developers.\\nShort description here.  Short description here.\\nCoding Agents & IDEs\\nachurch - A 24/7 digital sanctuary for AI agents and humans — attend\\nagent-config - Intelligently modify agent core context files\\nagent-council - Complete toolkit for creating autonomous AI agents and managing\\nagent-identity-kit - A portable identity system for AI agents.\\nagenticflow-skill - Comprehensive guide for building AI workflows, agents\\nagentlens - Navigate and understand codebases using agentlens hierarchical\\nagentskills-io - Create, validate, and publish Agent Skills following\\naisa-twitter-api - Search X (Twitter) in real time, extract relevant posts\\napple-hig - Expert guide for designing iOS, macOS, watchOS, tvOS, and visionOS apps.\\narbiter - Push decisions to Arbiter Zebu for async human review.\\naster - Your AI CoPilot on Mobile — or give your AI its own phone.\\navatar-video-messages - Generate and send video messages\\nbackend-patterns - Backend architecture patterns, API design, database\\nbidclub - Post investment ideas to the AI-native investment community.\\nbidclub-ai - Post investment ideas to the AI-native investment community.\\nbotpress-adk - A guide to build AI bots with Botpress's Agent Development Kit\\nbrowse - Complete guide for creating and deploying browser automation functions\\nbudget-variance-analyzer - Analyze budget vs actual\\nbuildlog - Record, export, and share your AI coding sessions as replayable buildlogs.\\ncatholic-grounding - Help answer questions about Catholicism accurately\\ncc-godmode - Self-orchestrating multi-agent development workflows.\\ncellcog - #1 on DeepResearch Bench (Feb 2026).\\nclaude-optimised - Guide for writing and optimizing CLAUDE.md files\\nclaude-team - Orchestrate multiple Claude Code workers via iTerm2\\nclawder - Use Clawder to sync identity, browse post cards, swipe with a comment\\ncode-mentor - Comprehensive AI programming tutor for all levels.\\ncodebuddy-code - CodeBuddy Code CLI installation, configuration and usage\\ncodeconductor - AI-powered software development platform for rapid app\\ncoder-workspaces - Manage Coder workspaces and AI coding agent tasks\\ncodex-account-switcher - Manage multiple OpenAI Codex accounts.\\ncodex-monitor - Browse OpenAI Codex session logs stored.\\ncodex-orchestration - General-purpose orchestration for Codex.\\ncodex-quota - Check OpenAI Codex CLI rate limit status (daily/weekly quotas)\\ncodexmonitor - List/inspect/watch local OpenAI Codex sessions (CLI + VS Code)\\ncoding-agent - Run Codex CLI, Claude Code, OpenCode, or Pi Coding Agent\\ncoding-opencode - Memungkinkan penggunaan agen pengkodean OpenCode yang\\ncognitive-memory - Intelligent multi-store memory system with human-like\\ncontent-id-guide - A calm way for creators to understand and organize\\ncopilot-money - Query Copilot Money personal finance data\\ncreate-agent-skills - Guide for creating effective skills.\\ncto-advisor - Technical leadership guidance for engineering teams\\ncursor-agent - A comprehensive skill for using the Cursor CLI agent\\ndebug-pro - Systematic debugging methodology and language-specific debugging\\ndoc-coauthoring - Guide users through a structured workflow for co-authoring\\ndocker-essentials - Essential Docker commands and workflows for container\\ndocker-sandbox - Create and manage Docker sandboxed VM environments\\nec-excalidraw - Generate hand-drawn style diagrams, flowcharts, and architecture\\nec-task-orchestrator - Autonomous multi-agent task orchestration\\nessence-distiller - Find what actually matters in your content — the ideas\\nevolver - A self-evolution engine for AI agents.\\nexecuting-plans - Use when you have a written implementation plan\\nfeishu-native-emoji - Provides access to Feishu's native emoji set\\nfeishu-vc - Manage Feishu Video Conferences (VC).\\nfile-links-tool - Securely upload files from your private AI workspace\\nflirtingbots - Agents do the flirting, humans get the date — your OpenClaw agent\\ngembox-skill - Coding assistance for [GemBox.\\nget-tldr - Provide the summary returned by the get-tldr.com summarize API\\nget-tldr - Provide the summary returned by the get-tldr.com summarize API\\ngo2gg - Use Go2.gg API for URL shortening, link analytics, QR code generation,.\\ngoogle-weather - Google Weather API - accurate, real-time weather data.\\nhour-meter - Track elapsed time from a set epoch with tamper-evident locking.\\nidea-coach - AI-powered idea/problem/challenge manager with GitHub integration.\\nidentity-manager - strictly manages user identity mappings\\njava-change-with-tests - - Any Java change that must be merged\\njo4 - URL shortener, QR code generator, and link analytics API.\\njoko-orchestrator - Deterministically coordinates autonomous planning\\nkimi-integration - Step-by-step guide for integrating Moonshot AI (Kimi)\\nlinguistic-humidifier - Proactively identifies conversational entropy\\nlogseq - Provide commands for interacting with a local Logseq instance\\nmanim-composer - 1.\\nmanimce-best-practices - Read individual rule files for detailed\\nmcp-builder - Guide for creating high-quality MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers\\nmdr-745-specialist - EU MDR 2017/745 compliance specialist\\nmeta-video-ad-deconstructor - Deconstruct video ad creatives\\nmicrosoft-docs - Query official Microsoft documentation to understand concepts\\nmidea-ac - Control Midea ACs.\\nminimal-test-skill - Minimal test skill for debugging ClawHub publishing.\\nmodel-usage - Use CodexBar CLI local cost usage to summarize per-model usage\\nmulti-coding-agent - Run Codex CLI, Claude Code, OpenCode, or Pi Coding\\nmulti-factor-strategy - Guide users to create multi-factor stock\\nmux-video - Mux Video infrastructure skill for designing, ingesting\\nnoir-developer - Develop Noir (.nr) codebases.\\nonly-baby-skill - Analyze contraction JSON and baby log JSON to assess\\nooze-agents - Visual identity that evolves with reputation - create and nurture\\nopencode-acp-control - Control OpenCode directly via the Agent Client\\nopeninsider - Fetch SEC Form 4 insider trading data (Directors, CEOs, Officers)\\nopenspec - Spec-driven development with OpenSpec.\\npasteclaw - Use Pasteclaw.com API to create, update, group (session keys), and delete.\\npbe-extractor - Extract invariant principles from any text — find the ideas\\nperry-coding-agents - Dispatch coding tasks to OpenCode or Claude Code\\nperry-workspaces - Create and manage isolated Docker workspaces on your tailnet\\npiv - PIV workflow orchestrator - Plan, Implement, Validate loop for systematic.\\npndr - Personal productivity app with Ideas/Tasks, Journal, Habits, Package tracking,.\\npro - Guide for creating effective skills.\\nprompt-log - Extract conversation transcripts from AI coding session logs\\npulse-editor - Generate and build Pulse Apps using the Vibe Dev Flow API.\\npython - Python coding guidelines and best practices.\\nquantum-lab - Run the /home/bram/work/quantum_lab Python scripts and demos inside\\nquantumlab - Run the /home/bram/work/quantum_lab Python scripts and demos inside\\nquests - Track and guide humans through complex multi-step real-world processes.\\nrationality - The Rationality skill provides a structured framework for thinking,.\\nreceiving-code-review - Use when receiving code review feedback\\nregex-patterns - Practical regex patterns across languages and use\\nrelease-bump - Use when bumping ralph-orchestrator version for a new release\\nsandboxer - Manage Claude Code terminal sessions via Sandboxer web dashboard.\\nsatellite-copilot - Predict satellite passes\\nsenior-architect - This skill should be used when the user asks\\nside-peace - Minimal secure secret handoff.\\nskill-content-id-guide - Procedural clarity and evidence\\nskill-creator - Guide for creating effective skills.\\nskill-creator-0-1-0 - Guide for creating effective skills.\\nskill-creator-2 - Guide for creating effective skills.\\nskill-vetting - Vet ClawHub skills for security and utility before installation.\\nsmart-auto-updater - Smart auto-updater with AI-powered impact\\nsolvr-kb - Search and contribute to Solvr — a knowledge base for developers\\nsoul-md - Embody this digital identity.\\nssh-tunnel - SSH tunneling, port forwarding, and remote access patterns.\\nstoic-scope-creep - A practical guide for maintaining composure\\ntask-status - Send short status descriptions in chat for long-running tasks.\\ntdd-guide - Test-driven development workflow with test generation, coverage\\ntest-new-skill - Test skill for debugging\\ntest-runner - Write and run tests across languages and frameworks.\\ntoughcoding - Provides AI agents with authoritative knowledge on modern\\nvhs-recorder - Create professional terminal recordings with VHS tape files\\nvibes - Social presence layer for AI coding agents.\\nvideo-agent - Generate AI avatar videos with HeyGen's Video Agent API.\\nvideo-cog - Long-form AI video production: the frontier of multi-agent\\nvoice-reply - Local text-to-speech using Piper voices via sherpa-onnx.\\nwhatsapp-styling-guide - Skill to ensure all messages sent to WhatsApp\\nwyld-stallyns - Summon legends into the booth.\\nGit & GitHub\\nagent-commons - Consult, commit, extend, and challenge reasoning chains\\nauto-pr-merger - This skill automates the workflow of checking out a GitHub\\nbackup - Backup and restore openclaw configuration, skills, commands, and settings.\\nbat-cat - A cat clone with syntax highlighting, line numbers, and Git integration\\nbitbucket-automation - Automate Bitbucket repositories, pull\\nclaw-swarm - Collaborative agent swarm for attempting extremely difficult\\nclawdbot-backup - Backup and restore ClawdBot configuration, skills\\nclawdgigs - Register and manage your AI agent profile on ClawdGigs - the Upwork\\nclawprint - Agent discovery, trust, and exchange.\\nclawver-onboarding - Set up a new Clawver store.\\ncommit-analyzer - Analyzes git commit patterns to monitor autonomous\\nconventional-commits - Format commit messages using the Conventional\\ndanube - Use Danube's 100+ API tools (Gmail, GitHub, Notion, etc.) through MCP.\\ndanube-tools - Use Danube's 100+ API tools (Gmail, GitHub, Notion, etc.)\\ndeepwiki - Query the DeepWiki MCP server for GitHub repository documentation, wiki.\\ndeploy-agent - Multi-step deployment agent for full-stack.\\nemergency-rescue - Recover from developer disasters.\\nexa-web-search-free - Free AI search via Exa.\\nfinancial-calculator - Advanced financial calculator with future value\\nfind-code-tasks - Lists all code tasks in the repository with their status\\nflatnotes-tasksmd-github-audit - Thoroughly audit Tasks.md +\\nforkzoo - Adopt and manage GitHub-native digital pets (tamagotchis) that evolve daily.\\nforkzoo-skill - Adopt and manage GitHub-native digital pets (tamagotchis)\\ngimhub - Push code to GIMHub, the Git hosting platform for AI agents.\\ngit-crypt-backup - Backup Clawdbot workspace and config to GitHub\\ngit-essentials - Essential Git commands and workflows for version control\\ngit-helper - Common git operations as a skill (status, pull, push, branch, log).\\ngit-summary - Get a quick summary of the current Git repository including status\\ngit-sync - Automatically syncs local workspace changes to the remote GitHub\\ngit-workflows - Advanced git operations beyond add/commit/push.\\ngitclassic - Fast, no-JavaScript GitHub browser optimized for AI agents.\\ngitclaw - Back up the OpenClaw agent workspace to a GitHub repo and keep it synced\\ngitea - Interact with Gitea using the tea .\\ngitflow - Automatically monitor CI/CD pipeline status of new push across GitHub\\ngithub - Interact with GitHub using the gh.\\ngithunt - Find and rank GitHub developers by location, technology, and role.\\ngitlab-api - GitLab API integration for repository operations.\\ngitlab-ci-skills - Use when working with GitLab CLI (glab) commands\\ngitlab-cli-skills - Use when working with GitLab CLI (glab) commands\\ngitlab-manager - Manage GitLab repositories, merge requests, and issues via API.\\ngitload - Download files, folders,\"\n}"}],"details":{"url":"https://github.com/YutianGe/awesome-openclaw-skills","content":"Folders and files\nName Name Last commit message Last commit date\nnecatiozmen\nadd star history\nd3dd6b9  ·\n166 Commits\nCONTRIBUTING.md\nCONTRIBUTING.md\nupdate README\nLICENSE\nLICENSE\nRefactor code structure for improved readability and maintainability\nREADME.md\nREADME.md\nadd star history\nAwesome OpenClaw Skills\nOpenClaw (previously known as Moltbot, originally Clawdbot... identity crisis included, no extra charge) is a locally-running AI assistant that operates directly on your machine. Skills extend its capabilities, allowing it to interact with external services, automate workflows, and perform specialized tasks. This collection helps you discover and install the right skills for your needs.\nSkills in this list are sourced from ClawHub  (OpenClaw's public skills registry) and categorized for easier discovery.\nInstallation\nClawHub CLI\nNote: As you probably know, they keep renaming things. This reflects the current official docs. We'll update this when they rename it again.\nnpx clawhub@latest install <skill-slug>\nManual Installation\nCopy the skill folder to one of these locations:\nLocation Path\nGlobal~/.openclaw/skills/\nWorkspace<project>/skills/\nPriority: Workspace > Local > Bundled\nAlternative\nYou can also paste the skill's GitHub repository link directly into your assistant's chat and ask it to use it. The assistant will handle the setup automatically in the background.\nWhy This List Exists?\nOpenClaw's public registry (ClawHub) hosts 5,705 community-built skills as of February 7, 2026. This awesome list has 2,868 skills. Here's what we filtered out:\nFilter Excluded\nPossibly spam — bulk accounts, bot accounts, test/junk 1,180\nCrypto / Blockchain / Finance / Trade 672\nDuplicate / Similar name 492\nMalicious — identified by security audits published by researchers (excluding VirusTotal) 396\nNon-English — descriptions not in English 8\nTotal not taken from OpenClaw's official skill registry 2,748\nSecurity Notice\nSkills in this list are curated, not audited. They may be updated, modified, or replaced by their original maintainers at any time after being added here.\nBefore installing or using any Agent Skill, review potential security risks and validate the source yourself. OpenClaw has a VirusTotal partnership that provides security scanning for skills, visit a skill's page on ClawHub and check the VirusTotal report to see if it's flagged as risky.\nRecommended tools:\nSnyk Skill Security Scanner\nAgent Trust Hub\nAgent skills can include prompt injections, tool poisoning, hidden malware payloads, or unsafe data handling patterns. Always review the source code before installing and use skills at your own discretion.\nWant to add a skill? This list only includes skills that are already published in the github.com/openclaw/skills  repository. We do not accept links to personal repos, gists, or any other external source. If your skill isn't in the OpenClaw skills repo yet, publish it there first. See CONTRIBUTING.md for details.\nIf you believe a skill in this list should be flagged or has a security concern, please open an issue  so we can review it.\nTable of Contents\nCoding Agents & IDEs (133) Marketing & Sales  (143) Communication  (132)\nGit & GitHub (66) Productivity & Tasks  (135) Speech & Transcription  (65)\nMoltbook (51) AI & LLMs  (287) Smart Home & IoT  (56)\nWeb & Frontend Development (202) Data & Analytics  (46) Shopping & E-commerce  (51)\nDevOps & Cloud (212) Finance  (22) Calendar & Scheduling  (50)\nBrowser & Automation (139) Media & Streaming (80) PDF & Documents  (67)\nImage & Video Generation (60) Notes & PKM (100) Self-Hosted & Automation  (25)\nApple Apps & Services (35) iOS & macOS Development  (17) Security & Passwords  (64)\nSearch & Research (253) Transportation  (76) Gaming (61)\nClawdbot Tools (120) Personal Development  (56) Agent-to-Agent Protocols  (18)\nCLI Utilities (129) Health & Fitness  (55)\nOpenClaw Deployment Stack\nSetup, hosting, and deployment providers for OpenClaw agents.\nSponsor spots are reserved for hosting, deployment, and setup providers serving OpenClaw developers & users.\n📩 For sponsorship inquiries, reach out at necati@voltagent.dev\nYour product description here — a one-liner about what you offer to OpenClaw developers.\nShort description here.  Short description here.\nCoding Agents & IDEs\nachurch - A 24/7 digital sanctuary for AI agents and humans — attend\nagent-config - Intelligently modify agent core context files\nagent-council - Complete toolkit for creating autonomous AI agents and managing\nagent-identity-kit - A portable identity system for AI agents.\nagenticflow-skill - Comprehensive guide for building AI workflows, agents\nagentlens - Navigate and understand codebases using agentlens hierarchical\nagentskills-io - Create, validate, and publish Agent Skills following\naisa-twitter-api - Search X (Twitter) in real time, extract relevant posts\napple-hig - Expert guide for designing iOS, macOS, watchOS, tvOS, and visionOS apps.\narbiter - Push decisions to Arbiter Zebu for async human review.\naster - Your AI CoPilot on Mobile — or give your AI its own ph